WEBVTT

00:00.770 --> 00:02.460
Let's talk about your pay.

00:02.680 --> 00:03.440
Huh?

00:03.910 --> 00:06.100
There's a lot involved with being a thane,

00:06.100 --> 00:09.320
but I'll pay you and provide your equipment.

00:10.780 --> 00:12.250
I'm...

00:12.250 --> 00:14.460
happy just to serve you...

00:14.460 --> 00:15.620
Not enough.

00:16.520 --> 00:20.440
There's something someone once told 
me over and over again, and that is:

00:20.440 --> 00:22.320
money is important.

00:22.320 --> 00:23.490
Right...

00:23.490 --> 00:26.320
If I didn't give you fair compensation,

00:26.320 --> 00:30.990
it could be interpreted as saying I 
don't value your work, or your loyalty.

00:32.410 --> 00:35.690
It may be in bad taste to 
put a price on everything,

00:36.300 --> 00:39.000
but money is always the clearest indicator.

00:39.980 --> 00:41.760
You are quite the grown-up.

00:44.020 --> 00:47.160
I'm just trying my hardest to be one.

00:55.280 --> 01:00.870
The Faraway Paladin

00:57.070 --> 01:00.870
<b><u>The Lord of the Rust Mountains</u></b>

02:18.110 --> 02:22.490
The Meaning of Courage

02:23.250 --> 02:24.740
You all right?

02:25.290 --> 02:27.640
I'm... just... fine!

02:28.160 --> 02:30.750
Great! One more lap, then!

02:30.750 --> 02:31.990
R-Right!

02:38.060 --> 02:43.760
<i>How hard did Blood, Mary, 
and Gus work to come up with ways</i>

02:43.760 --> 02:46.250
<i>to instill things in me so efficiently?</i>

02:47.770 --> 02:49.560
Last lap! Full strength!

02:49.560 --> 02:50.510
Right!

02:51.200 --> 02:53.780
<i>Regardless, I'll just keep doing my best</i>

02:53.780 --> 02:56.610
<i>so I can catch up to them someday.</i>

03:08.930 --> 03:10.290
Good effort.

03:10.490 --> 03:12.590
Do some light walking to catch your breath,

03:12.590 --> 03:14.420
and then we'll start muscle training.

03:14.420 --> 03:16.390
R-Right!

03:17.220 --> 03:20.480
Muscles are the most fundamental 
aspect of combat.

03:20.480 --> 03:23.630
As my master said, the brute 
force that muscles give you

03:23.630 --> 03:25.460
can solve most problems.

03:25.460 --> 03:26.200
Right!

03:35.500 --> 03:37.450
Okay, that's enough.

03:39.790 --> 03:41.810
That's it for your muscle training.

03:42.280 --> 03:44.600
I have to do this... every morning?

03:44.600 --> 03:46.810
Of course. We worked on your arms today,

03:46.810 --> 03:51.290
but we'll alternate focus on your 
legs, back, and other areas.

03:51.290 --> 03:52.820
That makes sense...

03:53.090 --> 03:56.300
I actually want to do some 
practice swings later,

03:56.300 --> 03:58.580
to check your footwork and body movements...

03:58.880 --> 04:00.250
Uh-huh...

04:00.250 --> 04:01.480
But first...

04:05.450 --> 04:07.530
I think you've met him before,

04:07.530 --> 04:09.920
but this is my friend, Menel.

04:09.920 --> 04:10.860
Hey.

04:10.860 --> 04:12.600
H-Hi...

04:14.030 --> 04:16.480
So, uh... I guess...

04:17.180 --> 04:19.860
I'm sorry for scaring you the other day.

04:22.380 --> 04:23.390
It's all right.

04:25.450 --> 04:28.950
Menel will be joining in your 
training sessions from now on.

04:28.950 --> 04:33.330
I'll also be asking him to work 
with you when I'm not around.

04:33.330 --> 04:36.290
R-Right! I appreciate your guidance!

04:36.770 --> 04:37.570
Sure.

04:38.260 --> 04:40.290
I need to go attend an assembly.

04:40.290 --> 04:44.050
After that, I'm going out to check 
on the people we treated before.

04:44.050 --> 04:45.820
I'll let you take over now.

04:45.820 --> 04:46.570
Sure.

04:48.620 --> 04:51.340
All right, let's start with practice swings.

04:51.340 --> 04:51.990
Right!

04:54.360 --> 04:56.490
I'll be counting on you, then.

04:56.490 --> 04:59.610
No problem. I'll take care of it.

05:01.660 --> 05:03.870
Hey, if it isn't our lord!

05:03.870 --> 05:06.450
Well... hello there.

05:19.340 --> 05:22.490
So, what were you doing at that pub?

05:23.170 --> 05:27.720
They were booked for a big 
celebration ten days from now,

05:27.720 --> 05:30.610
and they asked me to supply the meat for it.

05:30.610 --> 05:33.140
You hunt for a living, then?

05:33.140 --> 05:35.870
No, I work as a mercenary,

05:35.870 --> 05:40.160
but I can handle crossbows 
and traps to some extent.

05:40.160 --> 05:42.390
So it's like a side job?

05:42.390 --> 05:44.240
Something like that.

05:47.600 --> 05:49.060
Hurry up!

05:49.610 --> 05:51.320
That's right!

05:51.610 --> 05:53.280
Hey, watch where you're playing, boys.

05:53.280 --> 05:53.740
Okay!

05:54.180 --> 05:56.290
It's a fine city.

05:56.290 --> 05:57.080
Yes.

05:57.720 --> 06:00.740
People from many walks of life 
worked to make it that way.

06:04.170 --> 06:06.460
You know, paladin...

06:06.940 --> 06:07.770
Yes?

06:08.140 --> 06:12.710
I was once a warrior in 
service to the Iron Country.

06:13.400 --> 06:16.270
I was inexperienced as a fighter,

06:16.270 --> 06:20.260
so I was not granted the 
honor of dying with our king.

06:22.660 --> 06:24.860
To uphold our king's final command,

06:24.860 --> 06:29.430
we took up weapons and worked for 
many different employers to get by.

06:30.490 --> 06:33.110
Living in peace and contentment is not easy.

06:33.110 --> 06:37.560
We traveled across many 
lands before arriving here.

06:39.650 --> 06:43.970
Please give our young master 
the best guidance you can.

06:46.730 --> 06:47.520
I will.

06:50.360 --> 06:51.970
I swear on her light.

07:02.030 --> 07:04.720
Ru, is this your full strength?

07:08.600 --> 07:10.520
Surely you've got more than this in you!

07:12.630 --> 07:14.580
If this is your best...

07:18.450 --> 07:20.960
Okay, you lose.

07:21.760 --> 07:24.170
Getting used to pain is 
another part of training.

07:25.500 --> 07:29.040
H-How did you do that move you just did?!

07:29.040 --> 07:30.890
The one I just did?

07:31.300 --> 07:34.170
Hey, Menel, come here a sec.

07:34.170 --> 07:35.760
So you can experiment on me?

07:36.030 --> 07:38.530
He'll understand more easily 
if he sees it second-hand.

07:38.530 --> 07:41.140
S-Sorry for the trouble!

07:42.400 --> 07:43.470
Damn it...

07:43.770 --> 07:45.570
All right, fine.

07:45.570 --> 07:48.270
But you'd better make it a clean throw!

07:51.520 --> 07:52.400
<i>There.</i>

07:53.600 --> 07:56.950
<i>This should get Bishop 
Bagley to investigate.</i>

07:59.700 --> 08:04.040
The Fire of Black Calamity will 
break out in the Rust Mountains.

08:05.540 --> 08:07.190
The dragon is coming!

08:07.190 --> 08:09.290
Valacirca will destroy all!

08:09.550 --> 08:14.590
Although I detest this dragon power, 
you leave me with no choice!

08:15.920 --> 08:17.740
Tough scales,

08:18.560 --> 08:20.300
a massive body,

08:21.210 --> 08:24.150
born with the ability to use Words...

08:24.960 --> 08:27.490
The dragon, Valacirca.

08:28.470 --> 08:30.950
The dragon's power is 
second only to the gods'.

08:31.690 --> 08:35.310
When I fought the Echo of a god back then,

08:35.310 --> 08:37.170
I nearly died at one point.

08:37.980 --> 08:41.820
<i>Things were bad enough with 
just an Echo, and now...</i>

08:42.950 --> 08:44.900
An Echo and a dragon...

08:48.760 --> 08:50.400
I don't like this.

08:51.900 --> 08:53.150
I'm scared.

08:55.080 --> 08:56.780
Don't lose your nerve!

08:57.690 --> 08:59.330
Come on! One more round!

09:00.170 --> 09:03.190
Why would you hesitate to attack 
when I'm wearing armor?

09:03.610 --> 09:06.560
You're even more naïve than Will!

09:06.560 --> 09:09.570
What's wrong? Giving up already?

09:09.830 --> 09:13.310
Gonna run home with your tail 
between your legs, Young Master?

09:13.630 --> 09:15.650
I-I'm not done!

09:22.620 --> 09:24.780
You got me right in the head, 
and that's the hardest you can hit?

09:26.160 --> 09:29.660
Are those chunky arms just for show? Well?!

09:29.930 --> 09:32.590
Oh, yeah, you're clearly scared now.

09:32.590 --> 09:35.370
Gonna start crying and run away? Are ya?!

09:35.370 --> 09:37.040
I-I won't run!

09:37.040 --> 09:40.480
Then keep hitting! Put some 
force into it, you weakling!

09:49.200 --> 09:51.970
<i>I can always count on Menel.</i>

10:03.810 --> 10:06.370
You actually put some spirit into that one.

10:06.370 --> 10:07.510
Keep it up!

10:08.130 --> 10:10.510
Th-Thank you!

10:11.510 --> 10:12.760
<i>Incredible...</i>

10:13.380 --> 10:16.610
<i>I can see Ru getting stronger 
with each round of combat.</i>

10:20.020 --> 10:21.550
<i>Hey, Blood...</i>

10:22.470 --> 10:27.730
<i>Did you ever feel like this, I wonder?</i>

10:31.950 --> 10:33.320
Here you go.

10:33.760 --> 10:37.520
I don't... know if I can get this down...

10:37.520 --> 10:39.610
Your training will go to waste if you don't.

10:39.610 --> 10:41.590
Force it down if you have to.

10:41.590 --> 10:45.280
You need to take in more food than the 
amount you burn through activity.

10:45.700 --> 10:49.200
You can take it slow, but eat all of this.

10:49.200 --> 10:50.830
O-Okay...

10:59.580 --> 11:03.920
Um... Thank you again.

11:04.950 --> 11:06.130
For what?

11:06.810 --> 11:09.940
For accepting me as your thane,

11:09.940 --> 11:12.170
and for training me.

11:12.170 --> 11:17.020
You even pay me and give me 
food. I'm truly grateful.

11:19.020 --> 11:22.180
Um, are you aware of my background?

11:23.000 --> 11:25.710
I have a guess... I suppose.

11:27.330 --> 11:29.880
I was... well...

11:30.470 --> 11:34.160
born of noble blood within my clan.

11:34.560 --> 11:37.410
My parents died of illness 
while I was young,

11:37.410 --> 11:41.200
so the people of my clan shielded 
me from all hardships.

11:41.200 --> 11:42.800
So it seems.

11:42.800 --> 11:46.220
But I wondered if that was 
really the right way to live.

11:46.860 --> 11:52.030
Should the one who bears responsibility 
for his clan be so weak and cowardly?

11:54.690 --> 11:58.690
That was when I heard a song about you.

11:59.880 --> 12:04.600
I dearly wished that I could be like you.

12:05.120 --> 12:09.820
Being able to serve you now 
is like a dream come true.

12:09.820 --> 12:11.900
I'm so happy I can learn from you

12:11.900 --> 12:14.430
what it means to be a warrior, 
and what courage is.

12:16.040 --> 12:17.320
Thank you.

12:17.320 --> 12:21.590
I'll do everything in my power 
to be a worthy master for you.

12:22.780 --> 12:26.930
But I'm not so sure I can 
teach you what courage is.

12:26.930 --> 12:28.660
Um...

12:28.660 --> 12:31.740
I just mean I don't actually 
have that much courage.

12:31.740 --> 12:34.810
Even though you faced a 
wyvern and a chimera?

12:36.450 --> 12:41.710
Ru, can facing opponents you know you 
can defeat be called courageous?

12:42.890 --> 12:45.170
You knew you could defeat them?

12:45.170 --> 12:47.570
To give you a frank analysis 
of my combat strength...

12:47.570 --> 12:51.130
I'm overwhelmingly more powerful 
than a wyvern or chimera.

12:51.760 --> 12:54.580
I can kill them just using the 
movements I was trained in.

12:55.850 --> 12:59.590
Wyverns and chimeras don't scare me.

12:59.590 --> 13:03.590
Beating opponents you're not 
afraid of isn't courage.

13:04.220 --> 13:08.630
Then... just what is courage, exactly?

13:09.850 --> 13:12.840
I'd like to know the answer to that myself.

13:15.550 --> 13:20.860
How can I face an opponent that 
I have no hope of defeating?

13:29.910 --> 13:31.160
I'm back.

13:32.020 --> 13:33.620
Reystov!

13:33.620 --> 13:35.710
Welcome back. How did it go?

13:36.410 --> 13:39.110
Nothing seemed particularly out of place.

13:39.110 --> 13:42.870
Should I report my findings 
to Anna, as usual?

13:42.870 --> 13:44.580
Yes, please do.

13:46.770 --> 13:49.580
I had heard you took in a new thane.

13:57.440 --> 13:58.650
Your back's too hunched.

13:59.330 --> 14:01.250
Your shoulders fall too far forward.

14:01.250 --> 14:03.100
It makes you look like a wimp.

14:03.100 --> 14:07.740
Pull in your chin, straighten your 
back, and tighten your lips.

14:08.180 --> 14:10.180
Don't let your eyes dart around.

14:10.180 --> 14:13.110
Look at the eyes or mouth of 
the one you're speaking to.

14:13.570 --> 14:15.250
R-Right!

14:15.250 --> 14:18.270
Good. That's a bit better.

14:18.270 --> 14:20.770
I'm Reystov. What's your name?

14:20.770 --> 14:22.260
I-It's Ru.

14:22.260 --> 14:25.180
I see. And what do you think of William?

14:25.180 --> 14:27.270
I-I have great respect for him!

14:27.770 --> 14:32.220
Then don't do anything to harm 
his reputation as your master.

14:32.990 --> 14:36.950
Keep your back straight and your 
eyes facing forward at all times.

14:36.950 --> 14:38.380
R-Right!

14:38.680 --> 14:42.300
When you speak, do so with 
confidence, and choose your words.

14:42.300 --> 14:45.490
If you can't do that, 
stay silent. Understand?

14:45.490 --> 14:46.230
Yes!

14:46.930 --> 14:48.090
You don't mind, right?

14:48.090 --> 14:51.690
Not at all. I was going to 
ask for your help, actually.

14:51.690 --> 14:52.900
Good to hear.

14:53.660 --> 14:55.390
You said your name is Ru?

14:55.390 --> 14:58.380
I'll be butting into your training a bit.

14:58.380 --> 14:59.150
Right!

15:00.890 --> 15:03.670
Oh, right. Reystov...

15:04.150 --> 15:05.400
Yes?

15:05.400 --> 15:08.100
What do you think courage is?

15:10.880 --> 15:13.420
I don't know what you're thinking about,

15:13.860 --> 15:17.010
but as long as you're thinking 
like that, you'll never know.

15:17.570 --> 15:18.980
Yeah, you're right.

15:20.070 --> 15:23.380
<i>I kept an eye on the Rust 
Mountains for a while,</i>

15:23.380 --> 15:26.310
<i>but throughout summer and fall, 
they were as peaceful as could be.</i>

15:26.970 --> 15:29.460
<i>Just as the Lord of Holly promised,</i>

15:29.460 --> 15:31.950
<i>the forest was plentiful, 
which made everyone happy.</i>

15:32.520 --> 15:36.460
<i>They even held a festival when the 
time came for the wheat harvest.</i>

15:37.320 --> 15:41.970
<i>My third winter in 
Torch Port was drawing near.</i>

15:46.670 --> 15:47.590
Well done.

15:47.960 --> 15:49.600
That was very good.

15:49.960 --> 15:52.500
Th-Thank you!

15:54.760 --> 15:57.140
My lord! My lord!

16:02.040 --> 16:04.630
Sightings of undead were reported?

16:04.630 --> 16:06.450
I'm sorry this always happens.

16:06.450 --> 16:11.270
It's all right. I give priority 
to matters involving undead.

16:11.270 --> 16:13.270
What shall we do this time?

16:14.150 --> 16:15.660
Good question...

16:17.500 --> 16:21.130
Ru, I'm going to go handle 
this matter myself.

16:21.430 --> 16:22.970
Would you come with me?

16:22.970 --> 16:27.690
Y-Yes! I would be honored to accompany you!

16:37.870 --> 16:41.170
I've heard dwarf eyes can 
see even in darkness,

16:41.170 --> 16:43.180
but try not to rely too 
heavily on your sight.

16:43.180 --> 16:44.890
R-Right!

16:44.890 --> 16:47.580
Let's review. Where are we headed?

16:47.580 --> 16:50.710
To... Pillar Mound... in the west, right?

16:50.950 --> 16:53.500
It's where the most recent 
sighting was reported,

16:53.500 --> 16:56.980
but it's deep in the forest 
and hasn't been explored yet.

16:56.980 --> 16:57.720
Right.

16:58.200 --> 17:00.590
The main reason is the fog.

17:00.590 --> 17:04.660
Though no one knows if it's due to the 
geography or a magical barrier...

17:05.580 --> 17:07.220
Let's proceed with caution.

17:07.500 --> 17:08.460
Right.

17:17.490 --> 17:20.250
I-It's very eerie, isn't it?

17:21.140 --> 17:23.570
But also... magnificent.

17:35.450 --> 17:36.990
Sir Will?

17:36.990 --> 17:38.320
It's all right.

17:38.850 --> 17:40.360
Take a good look.

17:42.300 --> 17:43.320
What is it?

17:43.320 --> 17:45.390
A grave keeper, perhaps.

17:45.390 --> 17:46.820
Grave keeper?

17:47.260 --> 17:49.700
This is a burial site.

17:49.700 --> 17:52.100
It's a burial site?

17:52.440 --> 17:56.490
He's probably here to 
scare off grave robbers.

17:56.490 --> 17:58.920
And the fog is probably 
either a magical barrier

17:58.920 --> 18:01.350
or a contract with the land spirits.

18:01.890 --> 18:08.850
This place was probably created as a place 
of rest for loved ones who went on before.

18:12.750 --> 18:15.250
Please rest in peace.

18:27.660 --> 18:32.110
Um... So where was the undead, then?

18:32.110 --> 18:34.000
Considering this is a burial site,

18:34.000 --> 18:37.500
I'm beginning to think there's a good 
chance someone was just seeing things.

18:37.500 --> 18:41.820
But I would think undead are more 
likely to show up at burial sites.

18:41.820 --> 18:44.890
Why? They all received proper burials.

18:44.890 --> 18:45.700
Huh?

18:45.700 --> 18:47.840
It's people who have been 
killed and then concealed,

18:47.840 --> 18:49.680
or bodies left out in the open,

18:49.680 --> 18:51.770
who tend to receive the god 
of undead's blessing.

18:52.260 --> 18:56.030
Even the god of undead 
is kind, in his own way.

18:56.390 --> 18:59.210
The god of undead... is kind?

18:59.210 --> 19:02.100
He is kind. Terribly kind.

19:02.740 --> 19:06.050
Um... What do you mean by that?

19:06.620 --> 19:08.590
The god of undead, Stagnate,

19:08.590 --> 19:12.420
can't bear to see people die 
miserable, hopeless deaths.

19:12.800 --> 19:18.660
So he grants all dying creatures the 
right to overturn tragic deaths.

19:18.660 --> 19:20.720
But, um...

19:20.720 --> 19:23.930
Naturally, that kind of blessing 
is a real inconvenience to others.

19:25.900 --> 19:29.060
But still, he believes from 
the bottom of his heart

19:29.460 --> 19:33.230
that no one should have to die in misery,

19:33.230 --> 19:36.810
and if they do, they can overturn their 
death with the radiance of their soul.

19:37.550 --> 19:42.320
Um, Sir Will... You, uh, seem to 
know quite a lot about this...

19:42.790 --> 19:45.210
An Echo of Stagnate...

19:45.210 --> 19:48.590
Surely you've never met one of those, right?

19:48.590 --> 19:52.670
Have you had an encounter 
with a Herald, perhaps?

19:53.070 --> 19:55.200
Wh-Why won't you look at me?!

19:55.200 --> 19:57.080
Well, I mean... How do I put it...

19:59.860 --> 20:02.100
Don't just laugh!

20:03.470 --> 20:06.360
It really looks like someone 
was just seeing things.

20:06.360 --> 20:09.150
S-So our search was all in vain, then?

20:11.430 --> 20:12.630
Is that...

20:13.110 --> 20:14.890
Ru, this way.

20:18.470 --> 20:21.600
Is it an entrance to the 
interior of the mound?

20:22.560 --> 20:23.640
Let's check it out.

20:23.640 --> 20:24.490
Right.

20:28.750 --> 20:31.110
I don't see anything.

20:32.180 --> 20:33.160
Lumen.

20:32.210 --> 20:32.960
Light

20:34.500 --> 20:36.210
Burn, Flames

20:34.760 --> 20:36.600
Flammo Ignis.

20:37.700 --> 20:40.070
Ru, carry this one.

20:40.070 --> 20:40.630
Okay.

20:41.740 --> 20:44.150
Why did you use two types of light?

20:44.510 --> 20:47.650
When you go up against an 
opponent with no night vision,

20:47.650 --> 20:49.150
what do you target first?

20:50.270 --> 20:51.210
Right.

20:52.400 --> 20:53.810
Well, shall we go?

20:53.810 --> 20:54.740
Yes.

21:17.160 --> 21:19.830
Is this the innermost chamber?

21:19.830 --> 21:21.950
Yeah. Beyond here...

21:36.290 --> 21:37.380
<i>No!</i>

21:37.810 --> 21:38.980
<i>This is...</i>

21:48.550 --> 21:52.120
Welcome to my temporary dwelling place.

21:52.120 --> 21:54.200
Has it really been two years,

21:54.200 --> 21:56.160
warrior of the light?

21:56.570 --> 21:58.110
Stagnate...

23:35.760 --> 23:40.010
The Messenger in
the Burial Chamber
